(in a joyous blur as he nuzzled right against the point where Julian's finger met the glass.) '
() '
(In the days that followed, Pupi became an inseparable presence. He lived with Julian across) '
(his everyday phone usage. When Julian scrolled news feeds, Pupi trotted along the bottom edge,) '
(curiously peering at headlines. When Julian spent two uninterrupted hours doom-scrolling,) '
(Pupi yawned conspicuously, curled into a ball on the screen boundary, and fell asleep, softly) '
(reminding Julian how fast time was slipping away.) '
() '
(When Julian had to study, Pupi held up a tiny water droplet icon, gently barking with a speech) '
(reminder: 'Pupi thinks you should take a sip of water, Julian!' Julian would laugh, drink water,) '
(and watch Pupi do a victorious celebratory bounce. He wasn't an app to open and close;) '
(he was a loyal companion living in the margins of digital noise, bringing warmth to every unlock.) '
() '
(5. TASK 2 - FOUR-EMOTION ILLUSTRATION SPECIFICATION) '
(Requirements: Clean black-and-white line art, pure white background, 4 distinct expressions:) '
(1. HAPPY: Crescent closed eyes, perky upright floppy ears, wide joyful smile, radiant posture.) '
(2. SAD: Drooping long ears, large downcast watery pupils, small quivering mouth, single teardrop.) '
(3. ANGRY: Furrowed brow, tense sideways ears, adorable pouty grump expression, folded front paws.) '
(4. SURPRISED: Huge wide circular open eyes, ears perked high, exclamation marks, open 'O' mouth.) '
(All panels preserve identical character identity, proportions, and the PUPI collar tag.) '
() '
(6. TASK 3 - MULTI-PHONE ONLINE ARCHITECTURE MAP) '
(Scenario: Phone A feeds Pupi -> Backend validates & mutates state -> Phone B receives real-time update.) '
(Components:) '
(- Android Phone A: Optimistic UI, local Room DB, Pending Action Queue with client UUIDs.) '
(- Android Phone B: Subscribed via WebSocket, receives state updates, triggers reactive animation.) '
(- Backend API Gateway: Authenticates devices \\\(JWT Auth\\\), validates action idempotency.) '
(- Pet Management Service: Implements Optimistic Concurrency Control \\\(OCC\\\) with atomic version checks.) '
(- Cloud Database \\\(PostgreSQL / Supabase\\\): Stores pet state \\\(hunger, happiness, version\\\) & action logs.) '
(- WebSocket / MQTT Fanout Broker: Dispatches broadcast updates to all paired family devices.) '
() '
(Solutions to Technical Challenges:) '
(- Simultaneous Actions: Solved via OCC version checks \\\(WHERE id = ? AND version = ?\\\).) '
(- Offline Usage: Solved via Local Pending Queue in Room; synced on reconnection via WorkManager.) '
(- Duplicate Requests: Solved via Client Action UUID idempotency checks on backend.) '
(- Security & Privacy: Solved via Row-Level Security \\\(RLS\\\) restricting pairing to owner groups.) '
() '
(7. AI TOOLS & HONEST PROMPT EXPERIMENTATION LOG) '
(- Tool: Gemini / Claude for Architecture and Behaviour State Machine design.) '
(  Initial prompt asked for general AI virtual pet; refined to deterministic Finite State Machine) '
(  in pure Kotlin with discrete stat decay rules. Resulted in robust PupiBehaviorEngine.kt.) '
(- Tool: Imagen 3 for Character Expression line-art generation.) '
(  Initial prompts yielded colored 3D models with inconsistent dog breeds. Refined with explicit) '
(  negative constraints \\\('zero color, black and white line art only, identical collar and tag'\\\).) '
() '
(8. TESTING & COMPLIANCE SUMMARY) '
(- Functional Tests: Overlay permission, touch dragging, stat decay, and persistent Room DB.) '
(- Android Reliability: Handled background limits, screen rotation, and memory constraints.) '
ET

endstream
